  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency shelter and non-food item support to earthquake-affected populations in the Kunar and Nangarhar provinces of AfghanistanEmergency shelter and non-food item support to earthquake-affected populations in the Kunar and Nangarhar provinces of Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Severe earthquakes on 31 August and 4 September 2025 devastated eastern Afghanistan, particularly Kunar, Nangarhar, and Laghman provinces. Thousands of families are living in makeshift shelters or temporary displacement sites under harsh conditions. With winter approaching and temperatures in mountainous areas expected to drop below 0&#xb0;C. Vulnerable groups face increased exposure to the cold, health risks, and protection threats, while humanitarian response is hampered by limited operational capacity and inadequate basecamp facilities. IOM is providing Emergency Shelter and Non-Food Item (ESNFI) assistance to stabilize affected families and mitigate protection risks. Interventions include the distribution of emergency shelter kits, essential household NFIs, winterization support (blankets). Vulnerable households are prioritized, and activities are being coordinated with other ESNFI actors and local authorities to ensure equitable coverage, prevent duplication, and strengthen community resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
